README.OSK -- what this disk changed in C NewsOne file: libcnews/config.c, whose four directory names were blarson'sown (/h0/ulib/news, /h0/ulib/newsbin, /h0/spool/news).  They are now/h0/USR/LIB/CNEWS, /h0/CMDS/NEWS and /h0/SPOOL/CNEWS; libcnews/config.c.oriis the original.  NEWSCTL, NEWSBIN, NEWSPATH and NEWSARTS in theenvironment still override them, as C News intends.relaynews and libcnews.l build with the recipes in the project'stools/rebuild/recipes.psv.One file is ADDED: libosk/linkcopy.c, written for this collection.  RBFhas no hard links, and blarslib's ln.c, which supplies link() otherwise,makes one by writing directory sectors on the raw device -- its headersays "USE AT YOUR OWN RISK", and under os9exec it left C News's locklooking like a directory.  C News links only for its lock and forcross-posted articles, so linkcopy.c creates the second name exclusively(failing if it exists, which the lock depends on) and copies the file.relaynews links it ahead of blarslib.l.